@startuml
title Element lifecycle (bElem, bElemStats timers)
[*] --> Created : elementFactory / createByType
Created --> OnBoard : stepOnElement(cell)\nregisterLiveElement when it acts
state OnBoard {
  [*] --> Idle
  Idle --> Moving : moveInDirection\n(move timer)
  Moving --> Idle : timer done
  Idle --> Waiting : setWaiting / interacting
  Waiting --> Idle : timer done
  Idle --> Teleporting : steps into a teleporter
  Teleporting --> Idle : appears at the paired teleporter
}
OnBoard --> Collected : collect(): lifted into an inventory
Collected --> OnBoard : dropped (owner dies, dropsInventoryOnDeath)
Collected --> Disposed : used up (ammo, key in a door)
OnBoard --> Dying : hurt() to energy 0 / kill()\nqueued in toDispose
OnBoard --> Destroying : destroy() (explosion, missile)\nqueued in toDispose
Dying --> Destroying : destroyed while dying
Dying --> Disposed : kill timer done
Destroying --> Disposed : destroy timer done
OnBoard --> SwappedOut : its chunk goes to disk
SwappedOut --> OnBoard : the player comes back near
Disposed --> [*] : removed from board and live list
note right of OnBoard
  Elements far from the player
  (chamber::isActiveNear false) wait
  and run no mechanics().
end note
@enduml
